		<div id="m_textViewLayer" class="layer" style="z-index: 2; visibility: visible;">
			<div id="m_content" style="font-size: 100%; overflow-y: auto; direction: ltr; right: 20px;"><div><div id="m_topBuffer" style="height: 200px; display: none;"><img src="https://res.public.onecdn.static.microsoft/officeonline/hashed/79b48a07e8b20228/spiral.gif" class="loading" style="top: calc(50% + 20px);"></div><div id="pc1"><div style="height: 0px;"></div><div class="pageNumV2">1 / 32</div><div id="p1" name="p1"><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;">TOPIC : &nbsp;AI Fit Track API <br></span></b></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;"> <br></span></b></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;"> <br></span></b></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;">Team &nbsp; ID &nbsp;: &nbsp;</span></b><span style="direction:ltr;">SWTID-2026-4341<b><span style="direction:ltr;"> <br></span></b></span></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;">Team &nbsp; &nbsp;Leader : </span></b><span style="direction:ltr;">Nithya M, nithyamayavel58@gmail.com<b><span style="direction:ltr;"> <br></span></b></span></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;">Team Size: </span></b><span style="direction:ltr;">4<b><span style="direction:ltr;"> <br></span></b></span></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;"> <br></span></b></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;">TEAM &nbsp; MEMBERS: <br></span></b></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;"> <br></span></b></div><div style="overflow-y: auto; direction: ltr;"><div style="display: inline-block;"><table border="1" style="direction:ltr"><tbody><tr><th><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;">S.NO <br></span></b></div></th><th><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;">NAME <br></span></b></div></th><th><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;">MAIL ID <br></span></b></div></th></tr><tr><th><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;">1 <br></span></div></th><td><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;">NITHYA M <br></span></div></td><td><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;">nithyamayavel58@gmail.com <br></span></div></td></tr><tr><th><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;">2 <br></span></div></th><td><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;">MOULIKAA R <br></span></div></td><td><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;">moulikaar21@gmail.com <br></span></div></td></tr><tr><th><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;">3 <br></span></div></th><td><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;">NANDHINI A <br></span></div></td><td><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;">nandhu181206@gmail.com <br></span></div></td></tr><tr><th><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;">4 <br></span></div></th><td><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;">NANDHINI V <br></span></div></td><td><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;">nandhini29228@gmail.com <br></span></div></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;"> <br></span></b></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;"> <br></span></b></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;">INTRODUCTION: <br></span></b></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;"> <br></span></b></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;">AI Fit Track API is an application programming interface (API) designed to integrate <span style="direction:ltr;">Artificial Intelligence (AI) into fitness tracking and health monitoring applications. It <span style="direction:ltr;">helps users track their physical activities, monitor fitness progress, and receive <span style="direction:ltr;">personalized fitness recommendations based on their health data and activity levels. <br></span></span></span></span></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;">The AI Fit Track API can collect and process data such as daily steps, calories burned, <span style="direction:ltr;">workout duration, heart rate, and fitness goals. Using AI-based analysis, it can provide <span style="direction:ltr;">personalized workout suggestions, monitor fitness performance, and help users <span style="direction:ltr;">maintain a healthy lifestyle. <br></span></span></span></span></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;">The main objective of the AI Fit Track API is to make fitness tracking smarter, more <span style="direction:ltr;">efficient, and more personalized by providing intelligent insights and supporting users in <span style="direction:ltr;">achieving their fitness goals. <br></span></span></span></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;"> <br></span></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;"> <br></span></b></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;"> <br></span></b></div></div><hr class="pageHrV2"></div><div id="pc2"><div class="pageNumV2">2 / 32</div><div id="p2" name="p2"><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;">FitSense - Personalized fitness recommendations powered by AI. &nbsp; <br></span></b></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;">Description <br></span></b></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;"> <br></span></b></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;">The <b><span style="direction:ltr;">FitTrack AI &nbsp;</span></b><span style="direction:ltr;"> backend is a secure, scalable, and AI-powered RESTful application <span style="direction:ltr;">developed to simplify workout tracking and provide intelligent fitness <span style="direction:ltr;">recommendations. Built using <b><span style="direction:ltr;">Node.js</span></b><span style="direction:ltr;">, <b><span style="direction:ltr;">Express.js</span></b><span style="direction:ltr;">, <b><span style="direction:ltr;">MongoDB</span></b><span style="direction:ltr;">, and <b><span style="direction:ltr;">Mongoose</span></b><span style="direction:ltr;">, the <span style="direction:ltr;">backend exposes REST APIs that enable secure user authentication, workout <span style="direction:ltr;">management, workout searching, and AI-assisted fitness guidance. <br></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;">The application follows the <b><span style="direction:ltr;">Model-View-Controller (MVC)</span></b><span style="direction:ltr;"> architecture, making the <span style="direction:ltr;">project modular, maintainable, and scalable. User authentication is implemented using <b><span style="direction:ltr;">JSON Web Tokens (JWT)</span></b><span style="direction:ltr;">, while passwords are securely encrypted using <b><span style="direction:ltr;">bcrypt.js</span></b><span style="direction:ltr;"> <span style="direction:ltr;">before storage in MongoDB. Every protected API validates the JWT token through <span style="direction:ltr;">middleware before allowing access to sensitive resources. <br></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;">One of the key features of the project is its integration with <b><span style="direction:ltr;">Google Gemini AI</span></b><span style="direction:ltr;">, which <span style="direction:ltr;">provides personalized workout recommendations based on a user's age, fitness goals, <span style="direction:ltr;">and workout experience. The AI module also generates fitness insights by analyzing <span style="direction:ltr;">workout statistics such as total workouts completed, average workout duration, and <span style="direction:ltr;">calories burned. <br></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;">The backend returns standardized JSON responses, making it suitable for integration <span style="direction:ltr;">with web, mobile, and third-party applications. Proper error handling, input validation, <span style="direction:ltr;">route protection, and modular service implementation ensure the application is <span style="direction:ltr;">reliable, secure, and easy to extend. <br></span></span></span></span></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;">Scenario-Based Case Study <br></span></b></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;">Background <br></span></b></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;">Rahul is a fitness enthusiast who exercises regularly but records his workouts manually <span style="direction:ltr;">using notebooks and spreadsheets. Although he maintains consistency in his fitness <span style="direction:ltr;">routine, he finds it difficult to organize workout history, monitor progress, and determine <span style="direction:ltr;">whether his exercise habits align with his fitness goals. He also lacks professional <span style="direction:ltr;">guidance when deciding which workouts are best suited for his current fitness level. <br></span></span></span></span></span></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;"> <br></span></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;">Problem <br></span></b></div><ul style="margin-left:33px;"><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Difficulty maintaining a centralized record of workouts. <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Manual tracking leads to inaccurate workout history. <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· No secure user authentication for personal fitness records. <br></span></div></li></ul></div><hr class="pageHrV2"></div><div id="pc3"><div class="pageNumV2">3 / 32</div><div id="p3" name="p3"><ul style="margin-left:33px;"><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Unable to search previous workouts efficiently. <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· No personalized workout recommendations. <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· No insights regarding overall workout performance. <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Time-consuming manual calculation of calories burned and workout duration. <br></span></div></li></ul><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;">Solution <br></span></b></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;">The <b><span style="direction:ltr;">FitTrack AI &nbsp;</span></b><span style="direction:ltr;"> provides a centralized backend system where users can securely <span style="direction:ltr;">register, authenticate, and manage workout records. Users can add, update, delete, <span style="direction:ltr;">retrieve, and search workouts through RESTful APIs. By integrating <b><span style="direction:ltr;">Google Gemini AI</span></b><span style="direction:ltr;">, <span style="direction:ltr;">the application analyzes user information and workout statistics to generate intelligent <span style="direction:ltr;">workout recommendations and personalized fitness insights. <br></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;">The backend follows industry-standard security practices including JWT authentication, <span style="direction:ltr;">password hashing, middleware-based authorization, centralized error handling, and <span style="direction:ltr;">MongoDB schema validation. <br></span></span></span></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;">Usage <br></span></b></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;">User Usage <br></span></b></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;">A registered user can create an account using the registration endpoint and securely log <span style="direction:ltr;">in using email and password. After successful authentication, the backend generates a <span style="direction:ltr;">JWT token that authorizes access to protected APIs. <br></span></span></span></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;">Using authenticated APIs, users can: <br></span></div><ul style="margin-left:33px;"><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Create new workout records. <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· View all previously completed workouts. <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Retrieve a workout by its unique identifier. <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Update existing workout information. <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Delete unwanted workout records. <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Search workouts using workout name, category, or workout date. <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Generate AI-powered workout recommendations. <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Obtain AI-generated fitness insights based on workout statistics. <br></span></div></li></ul><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;"> <br></span></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;">AI Usage <br></span></b></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;">The AI module communicates with Google Gemini using a dedicated service layer. <br></span></div></div><hr class="pageHrV2"></div><div id="pc4"><div class="pageNumV2">4 / 32</div><div id="p4" name="p4"><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;">Users provide information such as: <br></span></div><ul style="margin-left:33px;"><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Age <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Fitness Goal <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Experience Level <br></span></div></li></ul><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;">Gemini processes this information and returns: <br></span></div><ul style="margin-left:33px;"><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Personalized workout plan <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Weekly exercise suggestions <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Beginner/Intermediate/Advanced recommendations <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Motivational guidance <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Safety tips <br></span></div></li></ul><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;">Similarly, users can submit workout statistics including: <br></span></div><ul style="margin-left:33px;"><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Total Workouts <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Average Workout Duration <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Total Calories Burned <br></span></div></li></ul><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;">The AI module analyzes these values and produces personalized fitness insights. <br></span></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;">Outcome <br></span></b></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;">The AI FitTrack backend significantly improves fitness tracking by eliminating manual <span style="direction:ltr;">record keeping and providing intelligent recommendations based on user activity. <span style="direction:ltr;">Secure authentication ensures that only authorized users can access personal workout <span style="direction:ltr;">data, while AI assistance helps users improve their exercise routines with personalized <span style="direction:ltr;">suggestions. <br></span></span></span></span></span></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;">The modular MVC architecture enables easy maintenance and future scalability. The <span style="direction:ltr;">application can later be extended with additional features such as nutrition tracking, <span style="direction:ltr;">BMI calculation, wearable device integration, workout reminders, and fitness analytics <span style="direction:ltr;">dashboards without major architectural changes. <br></span></span></span></span></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;"> <br></span></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;">1. Software Requirements <br></span></b></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;">The FitTrack AI &nbsp; requires the following software components for development and <span style="direction:ltr;">execution.<b><span style="direction:ltr;">Operating System:</span></b><span style="direction:ltr;"> Windows 10/11, macOS, or Linux (supports cross-<span style="direction:ltr;">platform operations). <br></span></span></span></span></div></div><hr class="pageHrV2"></div><div id="pc5"><div class="pageNumV2">5 / 32</div><div id="p5" name="p5"><ul style="margin-left:33px;"><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· <b><span style="direction:ltr;">Node.js (v16 or above):</span></b><span style="direction:ltr;"> Runtime ecosystem running server logic and routing <span style="direction:ltr;">infrastructure. <br></span></span></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· <b><span style="direction:ltr;">npm (v8 or above):</span></b><span style="direction:ltr;"> Node package manager to control operational <span style="direction:ltr;">dependencies. <br></span></span></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· <b><span style="direction:ltr;">Express.js:</span></b><span style="direction:ltr;"> Lightweight routing web framework to construct backend RESTful <span style="direction:ltr;">entry points. <br></span></span></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· <b><span style="direction:ltr;">MongoDB:</span></b><span style="direction:ltr;"> Document NoSQL engine storing users, posts, categories, <span style="direction:ltr;">comments, and analytics metrics. <br></span></span></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· <b><span style="direction:ltr;">Postman:</span></b><span style="direction:ltr;"> API verification toolkit to assert schema validation responses across <span style="direction:ltr;">administrative route shields. <br></span></span></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· <b><span style="direction:ltr;">Code Editor:</span></b><span style="direction:ltr;"> Visual Studio Code or similar IDE environment. <br></span></span></div></li></ul><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;">2. Hardware Requirements <br></span></b></div><ul style="margin-left:33px;"><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· <b><span style="direction:ltr;">Processor:</span></b><span style="direction:ltr;"> Intel Core i5 (8th Gen or above) / AMD Ryzen 5 or equivalent. <br></span></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· <b><span style="direction:ltr;">RAM:</span></b><span style="direction:ltr;"> 8 GB minimum (16 GB recommended for concurrent instances of <span style="direction:ltr;">MongoDB, processing layers, and execution nodes). <br></span></span></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· <b><span style="direction:ltr;">Storage:</span></b><span style="direction:ltr;"> 1 GB of available disk workspace. <br></span></span></div></li></ul><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;">Epic 1: Project Architecture <br></span></b></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;"> <br></span></div></div><hr class="pageHrV2"></div><div id="pc6"><div class="pageNumV2">6 / 32</div><div id="p6" name="p6"><div style="position: relative; height: 50.161px; width: 75px; overflow: hidden;"><img "="" id="pi6_0" width="98.2829864335686" style="position: absolute; top: -11.6394px; left: -11.6394px; clip: rect(11.6394px, 86.6394px, 61.8004px, 11.6394px); visibility: visible;" src="blob:https://word-edit.officeapps.live.com/b7144e04-2365-4e59-96f8-cc161db038ac"></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;"> <br></span></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;">The FitTrack AI &nbsp; follows a layered architecture based on the MVC (Modelâ€“Viewâ€“<span style="direction:ltr;">Controller) design pattern. The application separates routing, business logic, database <span style="direction:ltr;">interaction, middleware, and AI services into independent modules, making the project <span style="direction:ltr;">easier to maintain and scale. <br></span></span></span></span></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;">When a client sends an HTTP request, the Express server receives it and forwards it to <span style="direction:ltr;">the corresponding route. Protected routes first pass through the authentication <span style="direction:ltr;">middleware, which validates the JWT token before granting access. Controllers process <span style="direction:ltr;">validated requests and invoke business logic or AI services as required. Database <span style="direction:ltr;">interactions are handled through Mongoose models, while Google Gemini AI is <span style="direction:ltr;">accessed through a dedicated service layer. Finally, the controller returns a structured <span style="direction:ltr;">JSON response to the client. <br></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;">This layered approach improves modularity, security, and maintainability while ensuring <span style="direction:ltr;">that each component has a single responsibility. <br></span></span></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;">Overall Architecture Components <br></span></b></div><ul style="margin-left:33px;"><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Client Application (React / Mobile App / Postman) <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Express Server <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· API Routes <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Authentication Middleware <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Controllers <br></span></div></li></ul></div><hr class="pageHrV2"></div><div id="pc7"><div class="pageNumV2">7 / 32</div><div id="p7" name="p7"><ul style="margin-left:33px;"><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Services <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Google Gemini AI Service <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· MongoDB Database <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Mongoose Models <br></span></div></li></ul><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;">Each component communicates through well-defined interfaces, ensuring loose <span style="direction:ltr;">coupling and easier future enhancements. <br></span></span></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;">Components Definition <br></span></b></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;">The FitTrack AI &nbsp; follows a modular backend architecture in which every component <span style="direction:ltr;">performs a dedicated responsibility. The separation of concerns ensures <span style="direction:ltr;">maintainability, scalability, and efficient execution of requests. Each request passes <span style="direction:ltr;">through multiple layers before reaching the database or AI service, ensuring secure and <span style="direction:ltr;">reliable processing. <br></span></span></span></span></span></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;">1. Client Layer (Frontend/API Consumer) <br></span></b></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;">The Client Layer is the entry point of the application. It can be a React application, <span style="direction:ltr;">mobile application, or API testing tool such as Postman. The client sends HTTP requests <span style="direction:ltr;">to the backend server and receives JSON responses. <br></span></span></span></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;">Responsibilities <br></span></b></div><ul style="margin-left:33px;"><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Sends API requests. <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Displays workout information. <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Stores JWT token after login. <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Invokes AI recommendation APIs. <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Displays success and error responses. <br></span></div></li></ul><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;">APIs Accessed <br></span></b></div><ul style="margin-left:33px;"><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Authentication APIs <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Workout APIs <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· AI Recommendation APIs <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· AI Fitness Insight APIs <br></span></div></li></ul><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;">2. Express Server Gateway <br></span></b></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;">The Express server acts as the central gateway of the application. It listens for incoming <span style="direction:ltr;">requests, configures middleware, parses request bodies, enables CORS, and routes <span style="direction:ltr;">requests to the appropriate controllers. <br></span></span></span></div></div><hr class="pageHrV2"></div><div id="pc8"><div class="pageNumV2">8 / 32</div><div id="p8" name="p8"><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;">Responsibilities <br></span></b></div><ul style="margin-left:33px;"><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Starts HTTP server <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Parses JSON requests <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Enables Cross-Origin Resource Sharing (CORS) <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Registers application routes <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Connects middleware <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Handles centralized errors <br></span></div></li></ul><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;">Example Responsibilities <br></span></b></div><ul style="margin-left:33px;"><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Receive HTTP Request <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Validate Request Format <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Forward Request to Routes <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Return JSON Response <br></span></div></li></ul><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;">3. Authentication Middleware <br></span></b></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;">Authentication middleware protects all secured APIs by validating the JSON Web Token <span style="direction:ltr;">(JWT). Every protected request must include a valid Authorization header. <br></span></span></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;">Responsibilities <br></span></b></div><ul style="margin-left:33px;"><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Read Authorization Header <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Extract JWT Token <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Verify JWT Signature <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Decode User Information <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Attach User Information to Request <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Reject Unauthorized Requests <br></span></div></li></ul><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;">Benefits <br></span></b></div><ul style="margin-left:33px;"><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Prevents unauthorized access <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Secures workout information <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Allows only authenticated users to access protected APIs <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Eliminates repeated authentication logic inside controllers <br></span></div></li></ul><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;">4. Route Layer <br></span></b></div></div><hr class="pageHrV2"></div><div id="pc9"><div class="pageNumV2">9 / 32</div><div id="p9" name="p9"><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;">Routes define the application's API endpoints and map incoming HTTP requests to <span style="direction:ltr;">controller methods. Each route represents a specific functionality of the system. <br></span></span></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;">Authentication Routes <br></span></b></div><ul style="margin-left:33px;"><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Register User <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Login User <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· User Profile <br></span></div></li></ul><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;">Workout Routes <br></span></b></div><ul style="margin-left:33px;"><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Add Workout <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Get All Workouts <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Search Workouts <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Get Workout by ID <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Update Workout <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Delete Workout <br></span></div></li></ul><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;">AI Routes <br></span></b></div><ul style="margin-left:33px;"><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Workout Recommendation <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Fitness Insights <br></span></div></li></ul><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;">5. Controller Layer <br></span></b></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;">Controllers contain the application's business logic. They receive requests from routes, <span style="direction:ltr;">validate input data, invoke services or database operations, and generate standardized <span style="direction:ltr;">JSON responses. <br></span></span></span></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;">Authentication Controller <br></span></b></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;">Responsible for: <br></span></div><ul style="margin-left:33px;"><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· User Registration <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· User Login <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· User Profile Retrieval <br></span></div></li></ul><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;">Workout Controller <br></span></b></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;">Responsible for: <br></span></div><ul style="margin-left:33px;"><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Creating Workout Records <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Retrieving Workout Records <br></span></div></li></ul></div><hr class="pageHrV2"></div><div id="pc10"><div class="pageNumV2">10 / 32</div><div id="p10" name="p10"><ul style="margin-left:33px;"><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Updating Workouts <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Deleting Workouts <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Searching Workouts <br></span></div></li></ul><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;">AI Controller <br></span></b></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;">Responsible for: <br></span></div><ul style="margin-left:33px;"><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Sending prompts to Google Gemini <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Receiving AI-generated recommendations <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Returning AI responses to clients <br></span></div></li></ul><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;">6. Service Layer <br></span></b></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;">The Service Layer contains reusable business logic that can be shared among multiple <span style="direction:ltr;">controllers. <br></span></span></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;">Gemini AI Service <br></span></b></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;">Responsible for: <br></span></div><ul style="margin-left:33px;"><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Preparing prompts <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Sending prompts to Google Gemini <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Receiving AI-generated responses <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Returning formatted recommendations <br></span></div></li></ul><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;">JWT Service <br></span></b></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;">Responsible for: <br></span></div><ul style="margin-left:33px;"><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Creating JWT Tokens <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Configuring Token Expiry <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Verifying User Identity <br></span></div></li></ul><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;">Password Service <br></span></b></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;">Responsible for: <br></span></div><ul style="margin-left:33px;"><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Hashing Passwords <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Comparing Passwords During Login <br></span></div></li></ul><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;">7. Database Layer <br></span></b></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;">MongoDB stores all persistent application data. Mongoose acts as an Object Data <span style="direction:ltr;">Modeling (ODM) library that simplifies communication between Node.js and MongoDB. <br></span></span></div></div><hr class="pageHrV2"></div><div id="pc11"><div class="pageNumV2">11 / 32</div><div id="p11" name="p11"><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;">Collections <br></span></b></div><ul style="margin-left:33px;"><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Users Collection <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Workouts Collection <br></span></div></li></ul><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;">Advantages <br></span></b></div><ul style="margin-left:33px;"><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Flexible Schema <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· High Performance <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Easy Data Retrieval <br></span></div></li><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· Scalable Architecture <br></span></div></li></ul><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;">Entity Relationship (ER) Diagram Description <br></span></b></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;">The AI FitTrack backend consists of two primary collections that are logically connected <span style="direction:ltr;">through a one-to-many relationship. <br></span></span></div><div style="position: relative; height: 50.1114px; width: 75px; overflow: hidden;"><img "="" id="pi11_0" width="98.2829864335686" style="position: absolute; top: -55.7207px; left: -11.6394px; clip: rect(55.7207px, 86.6394px, 105.832px, 11.6394px); visibility: visible;" src="blob:https://word-edit.officeapps.live.com/f8a7ce1a-68cf-4365-bda7-7e11596ad41d"></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;"> <br></span></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;">1. User Entity <br></span></b></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;">The User entity stores authentication and profile information. <br></span></div><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;">Attributes <br></span></b></div><div style="overflow-y: auto; direction: ltr;"><div style="display: inline-block;"><table border="1" style="direction:ltr"><tbody><tr><th><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;">Field</span></b><span style="direction:ltr;"> <br></span></div></th><th><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;">Type</span></b><span style="direction:ltr;"> <br></span></div></th><th><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;">Description</span></b><span style="direction:ltr;"> <br></span></div></th></tr></tbody></table></div></div></div><hr class="pageHrV2"></div><div id="m_endBuffer" style="height: 200px;"><img src="https://res.public.onecdn.static.microsoft/officeonline/hashed/79b48a07e8b20228/spiral.gif" class="loading"></div></div></div>
